    "details": "<p><strong>About the Hackathon:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Anyone can build an AI demo that works once. Agents that act. Systems that answer. is about what happens when it goes wrong. It's a free, 3-day virtual hackathon for student builders, hosted by StudentChakra and co-hosted by Priyanshu Agarwal (founder of NextMove, organiser of Hackorizon).</span></p>\n<p><strong>What You'll Build:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An agentic AI system for a real person with a real task. Start with a person, not an industry: who are they, what do they hate doing, what does your agent do for them, and where does it break? Solo or in a team of up to 4. No experience required.</span></p>\n<p><strong>How Projects Are Judged:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We judge how your project behaves when things go wrong:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Failure modes: how does it break?</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Human oversight: who stays in the loop?</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Intervention: can someone stop it?</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Reversibility: can a mistake be undone?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plus usefulness to a real person and the quality of your working build.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Prizes:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">$680 in prizes: 1st place about $500 in Apify credits; 2nd and 3rd place Cursor subscriptions.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Judges:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Experts from AI governance, cybersecurity, venture and OpenAI, including Dr. Esona Fomuso (formerly VP of Technology, JPMorgan Chase), Dr. Aleem Khalid Alvi (Professor of Cybersecurity &amp; Software Engineering, Sheridan College), Kunal Kapoor (Venture Continuity, Katha) and Priyanshu Agarwal (ChatGPT Lab, OpenAI India).</span></p>\n<p><strong>Key Dates:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Registration closes: Nov 27</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hackathon: Nov 28&ndash;30 (virtual)</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Final results: Dec 8</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who Can Join:</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Students worldwide, solo or in teams of 1&ndash;4. Free.</span></p>",
